# Responsive layouts (no half-ass breakpoints)

UI must be **designed per breakpoint**, not a phone stack stretched until it looks sparse. If a wide viewport could belong to an unfinished mock, the layout failed.

## Shell vs composition (do not conflate)

- **Shell discipline (keep):** Home and tools share the same product **width** via [`PAGE_SHELL`](src/lib/constants/page-shell.ts) — do not let `/` become a stray wider *frame* than guides/tools.
- **Composition (required):** Same shell ≠ same sparse single column. Marketing may use asymmetric grids, full-bleed atmosphere bands, and a secondary visual zone. Workspaces stay paired panels. Filling `wide` is mandatory; matching tools’ *visual density* is not.

**Public Comms workshop journey / terminology:** [`comms-public-ux.mdc`](comms-public-ux.mdc). **Marketing / Home effort bar:** [`public-marketing-ux.mdc`](public-marketing-ux.mdc). Stale “leave density as-is” or “landing SHIPPED” notes may be revised when they block intentional breakpoint compositions.

## Page shell scale (required)

Use [`PageShell`](src/components/layout/PageShell.tsx) / [`PAGE_SHELL`](src/lib/constants/page-shell.ts) — do not invent one-off `max-w-*` for page frames.

| Tier | Class | Use |
|------|--------|-----|
| `chrome` | `max-w-[100rem]` (~1600px) | Header, footer, hub nav/banner only |
| `wide` | `max-w-[90rem]` (~1440px) | Home, examples, multi-panel tools/workspaces, guide indexes (default) |
| `read` | `max-w-3xl` | Guide chapters, privacy, long-form → prefer [`GuideLayout`](src/components/comms/GuideLayout.tsx) |
| `focus` | `max-w-2xl` | Manifesto, public forms — **not** multi-panel workspaces |
| `nestedFocus` | `max-w-2xl` (no extra px) | Hub forms already inside `/app` `wide` (forgot/reset/invite) |
| `nestedAuth` | `max-w-md` (no extra px) | Hub login / MFA |
| `nestedProfile` | `max-w-lg` (no extra px) | Hub profile |

Chrome and wide use `px-4 sm:px-6 xl:px-8`. Nested Hub tiers omit horizontal padding so they do not double-pad inside `PAGE_SHELL.wide`. After picking a shell, compose with grids/columns at `lg`/`xl`/`2xl` — do not leave a sparse single column on a 90rem shell (Brand Kit is the reference **workspace** pattern; Home marketing follows [`public-marketing-ux.mdc`](public-marketing-ux.mdc)).

## Reference compositions

- **Home** — see [`public-marketing-ux.mdc`](public-marketing-ux.mdc). Short form: at `lg+`, two-zone hero inside `wide` (message + secondary visual earning ≥~40% of content width); body keeps trust `Callout`, Brand Kit link row, denser channel lists. Full-bleed gradient alone is atmosphere, not a secondary zone. Docs saying “landing shipped” do **not** freeze a layout that fails the empty-half / unfinished-mock test.
- **Guides** — `GuideLayout`: related links as a compact nav row (never a fat empty tinted card); steps/sections with left accent or markers; optional horizontal step progress (see social-media-plan). Guide **index** (`/guide`) uses `GuideLayout size="wide"` with a path grid + two-column chapters
- **Tools** — canvas tools use [`ToolEditorLayout`](src/components/tools/ToolEditorLayout.tsx) — see [`tool-editor-ux.mdc`](tool-editor-ux.mdc) for editor chrome + face uplift
- **Brand Kit / workspaces** — `PageShell` **wide** with paired panels at `lg+`; utility actions near the heading
- **Hub auth** — `nestedAuth` / `nestedFocus` inside app layout — never a second `focus` shell with its own `px-*`
- **Short notes** — [`Callout`](src/components/ui/Callout.tsx), not default `Card`

Within a shell, still constrain body copy (`max-w-prose` / `max-w-xl`) when needed — **constrain the text measure, not the whole hero band to that measure without a counterweight.**

## Hard rejects (fix before shipping)

- **Stray wide home** — marketing/home *frame* wider than tools/guides without a documented shell change
- **Shell as alibi** — citing “same product width” to leave Home as a left-pinned stack on a full-bleed band
- **Empty-half hero** — full-bleed (or `wide`) hero whose only children are mark + `max-w-*` prose with no secondary visual zone at `lg+`
- **Gradient-as-product** — Brand Kit gradient (or abstract wash) treated as the dominant visual with no product UI, preview, or real imagery
- **Workspace on focus** — multi-panel settings (Brand Kit-class) stuck at `max-w-2xl` while chrome is ~100rem
- **Stretched mobile shell** — same single column, left-pinned blocks, growing empty space as the viewport widens
- **Orphan empty containers** — full-width cards whose content is a short left-aligned list with a dead zone filling the rest
- **Unbounded measure** — body copy running >~65–75ch without a readable constraint
- **Breakpoint blindness** — only `px-4` + `max-w-*` and no intentional change at `sm` / `md` / `lg` / `xl`
- **CTA row as afterthought** — buttons left-dumped with no wrap/stack plan across widths
- **Repeated hero CTAs** — same primary action three times down the page

## Do this instead

1. **Pick a shell tier first**, then compose for desktop / stack for mobile
2. **Fill or constrain** — use the width (grid/columns/rail) or shrink the surface; never a wide empty card or half-empty full-bleed
3. **Chrome vs body** — chrome may be `100rem`; page body uses `wide`/`read`/`focus`. Full-bleed **paint** is OK; content inside still fills or constrains
4. **Verify four widths** — ~375, ~768, ~1280, ~1536: each must look intentional (spot-check 1920 gutters; densify at `xl`/`2xl`, do not only grow margins)

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — multi-panel workspace on focus / orphan path card / empty-half hero
<PageShell size="focus">…
<Card><ul><li>One link</li></ul></Card>
<section className="w-screen"><div className="max-w-xl">…mark + copy only…</div></section>

// ✅ GOOD
<PageShell className="py-8 md:py-12">…
<div className="grid gap-4 lg:grid-cols-2">…
{/* Home lg+: message column + secondary visual zone */}
<GuideLayout title="…" relatedLinks={[…]} relatedLabel="Also see">…
```

## Checklist (any new/changed page or major layout)

- [ ] Shell tier matches page type (`wide` / `read` / `focus`)
- [ ] Desktop is not just mobile with more margin
- [ ] No full-bleed empty regions inside bordered/filled surfaces
- [ ] At ~1280 / ~1536, marketing heroes do not read as half-empty (secondary zone or intentionally constrained band)
- [ ] Body measure stays readable
- [ ] Spot-checked phone / tablet / desktop / xl (~1536)
